# NOT a complete .env template.
#
# This repo has never carried one — the real .env holds production secrets and is
# maintained by hand on each host. Do NOT copy this file to .env and expect the app
# to boot: it has no APP_KEY, no database settings, nothing but the block below.
#
# It exists only to document the one variable JARVIS needs, because that variable
# is shared with a separate program and has to be discoverable from this repo.
# Everything about the API itself is in docs/JARVIS_API.md.

# JARVIS — read-only assistant API (app/Http/Middleware/JarvisToken.php).
# Leave EMPTY to switch the whole API off: with no token, not one /api/jarvis route
# is registered, so there is nothing to probe. To enable it, generate a long random
# value and put the SAME value in JARVIS's own .env:
#   php -r "echo bin2hex(random_bytes(32));"
JARVIS_API_TOKEN=
